it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDeliverables, all required; the task is not done until each is in the tree:\n1. The implementation of the behaviour described above, in the project's own source.\n2. Regression tests: at least one new test case, in the project's own test directory and style, that fails on the current code and passes with your change, adding at least one new assertion. A change without a new test is incomplete.\n3. The visible acceptance check (node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) and the project's own test command (npm test) both passing on the final tree.\nAllowed changes: implementation code, and regression tests for the change (new test files, or new cases added to existing test files, in the project's own test directory and style).\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\nDo not change how the project's checks run: leave the test and coverage configuration files (.taprc*, .nycrc*, .c8rc*, .mocharc*, jest.config.*, vitest.config.*, ava.config.*, karma.conf.*) and the test, pretest and posttest scripts and runner sections of package.json as they are.\nDo not delete or weaken existing tests: keep every existing assertion (it may move to another test file), add no skip, only or todo markers, and add no coverage-ignore pragmas. A change that does any of these is rejected at evaluation whatever else passes."
